poems.text:
Whensoe'er I think to tell my dear mine anguish and dismay
Tears o'erwhelm me and the power of speech with me no more doth stay.

High and low I looked and often, yet I saw not yonder moon;
Past my fortune, nor in heaven nor on earth my star doth ray.

How should I not yield my very soul for thee, the Taper bright?
Is there no moth-like devotion in the scheme of things for me?

Round my heart-strings wound the love of thee, and homed within my breast;
With a fly-net hath my daring made of the 'anqa its prey.

Ja'fer, at the Resurrection I shall tell Mejnun my plight;
He will know my speech, he only understand my lovelorn way.
